### Why Fully Local AI Works Here

| Concern | Answer |
|---------|--------|
| **"Won't local LLM be too slow?"** | Phi-3-mini INT4 on modern CPU: **5-15 seconds per response**. For a help assistant (not a real-time chat), this is acceptable — users expect a moment while the AI "thinks." A typing indicator makes this feel natural. |
| **"Won't 2.5 GB model be too large?"** | Your published web app (`web-publish.zip`) is already 112 MB. The model ships as a downloadable asset on first run (or can be pre-bundled). It loads lazily — zero impact on startup until first help request. |
| **"Quality vs. GPT-4?"** | For **grounded, document-based Q&A** (not open-ended creativity), Phi-3-mini with RAG context performs excellently. It's answering from YOUR docs, not making things up. The retrieval layer ensures accuracy. |
| **"RAM requirements?"** | INT4 quantized Phi-3-mini: **~3-4 GB RAM** during inference. Your ERP server should have this headroom. Embedding model adds ~200 MB. |

