### Component 3: Local ONNX AI Engine

#### [NEW] `Infrastructure/AI/OnnxEmbeddingService.cs`
**Singleton** — semantic search embeddings:
- Loads `all-MiniLM-L6-v2.onnx` (23 MB, 384-dim embeddings)
- `Microsoft.ML.OnnxRuntime.InferenceSession` — thread-safe
- Interface: `Task<float[]> EmbedAsync(string text)` + `Task<float[][]> EmbedBatchAsync(string[] texts)`
- Lazy initialization — loaded on first call, not at startup
- Normalizes output vectors for fast cosine similarity (pre-computed norms)

#### [NEW] `Infrastructure/AI/WordPieceTokenizer.cs`
Tokenizer matching the embedding model's vocabulary:
- Loads `vocab.txt` (30,522 WordPiece tokens)
- `[CLS]` + tokens + `[SEP]` framing
- Subword splitting with `##` prefix convention
- Outputs `input_ids`, `attention_mask`, `token_type_ids` as `long[]`
- Max sequence length: 128 tokens (truncate + pad)

#### [NEW] `Infrastructure/AI/VectorIndex.cs`
In-memory vector similarity index:
- `ConcurrentDictionary<string, (float[] Embedding, DocumentChunkMetadata Meta)>`
- Cosine similarity via pre-normalized dot product
- Top-K retrieval: `Search(float[] query, int topK, float minThreshold = 0.3f)`
- Binary serialization: `Save(string path)` / `Load(string path)` for startup cache
- `ReaderWriterLockSlim` for concurrent read / exclusive write
- Incremental add/remove without full rebuild

#### [NEW] `Infrastructure/AI/LocalLlmService.cs`
**Singleton** — local text generation via Phi-3-mini ONNX:
```csharp
public sealed class LocalLlmService : IDisposable
{
    private readonly Model _model;        // Microsoft.ML.OnnxRuntimeGenAI.Model
    private readonly Tokenizer _tokenizer;
    private readonly SemaphoreSlim _gate = new(1, 1); // One inference at a time
    
    public bool IsModelLoaded { get; private set; }
    
    public async Task<string> GenerateAsync(string systemPrompt, string userPrompt, 
        int maxTokens = 512, float temperature = 0.3f, CancellationToken ct = default)
    {
        await _gate.WaitAsync(ct);
        try
        {
            // Build prompt in Phi-3 chat format:
            // <|system|>\n{systemPrompt}<|end|>\n<|user|>\n{userPrompt}<|end|>\n<|assistant|>
            var prompt = FormatChatPrompt(systemPrompt, userPrompt);
            var sequences = _tokenizer.Encode(prompt);
            
            var generatorParams = new GeneratorParams(_model);
            generatorParams.SetSearchOption("max_length", maxTokens);
            generatorParams.SetSearchOption("temperature", temperature);
            generatorParams.SetInputSequences(sequences);
            
            var output = _model.Generate(generatorParams);
            return _tokenizer.Decode(output[0]);
        }
        finally { _gate.Release(); }
    }
    
    // Streaming variant for SignalR real-time display
    public async IAsyncEnumerable<string> GenerateStreamingAsync(
        string systemPrompt, string userPrompt, 
        [EnumeratorCancellation] CancellationToken ct = default)
    {
        // Token-by-token generation using Generator class
        // Each token yielded immediately for real-time UI
    }
}
```

Key characteristics:
- **Lazy loading** — model loaded on first help request, not at app startup
- **Serialized inference** — `SemaphoreSlim(1,1)` prevents concurrent generation (single-threaded GPU/CPU inference is faster than competing threads)
- **Configurable** — if model files aren't present, `IsModelLoaded = false` and system falls back to templates
- **Streaming** — tokens streamed via `IAsyncEnumerable` for real-time SignalR display

#### [NEW] `Infrastructure/AI/IntentClassifier.cs`
ML.NET-trained multi-class classifier:
- Intents: `HowTo`, `Explain`, `Navigate`, `Troubleshoot`, `Search`, `Greeting`, `Farewell`, `Unknown`
